  "interpretation": "The point estimate missed by 295.14 s; the observed work components explain most of this: on the 12 matched rows the forecast projected 176.45 s of 64-position teacher forcing versus 72.45 s measured, and 284.31 s of free-run work versus 215.47 s measured. The separate Pytest cap4096 row projected 294.61 s using 4095 replays but stopped normally after 2380 emitted tokens / 2379 replays and took 179.62 s. Actual measured load plus trace preparation was 89.72 s, essentially equal to the 89.73 s fixed forecast; fixed setup did not explain the miss. Inference, not a measured causal attribution: forecast decode used context-length scaling and expected historical stop lengths; actual decode throughput at full prompt length did not follow the linear context proxy, and per-seed free-run stops shifted. Teacher-forcing timing also varied markedly across repeated same-prompt seed rows, so the single-source timing proxy did not predict the measured batch well. These are diagnostic timings and do not imply serving performance or semantic quality.",
